  "label": "Genome Scale Metabolic Modeling",
  "related": [
    "networks-cycles-e4e1",
    "metabolic-topic-372f",
    "computational-lymphangion-493f"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [
    "metabolomics"
  ],
  "slug": "telomere-genome-63e9",
  "summary": "New preprints extend curated GEMs and ME-models and add ML for essentiality and flux inference, alongside a benchmark of EC number prediction from reaction structures.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the construction and extension of genome-scale metabolic frameworks and their coupling to data-driven inference. iJL1143 for Fusarium venenatum A3/5 was built from an A. niger template via rule-based curation and checked against batch fermentation biomass data. coralME v1.3 widens ME-model scope to non-canonical amino acid translation, protein and RNA degradation, arbitrary coupling coefficients, and cofactor essentiality. Machine-learning methods are newly applied on top of these models: HyperGenie uses directed hypergraph neural networks on wild-type flux features to predict bacterial gene essentiality, and Flux Transformer infers mass-balanced fluxes from isotope labeling and measured rates. A systematic review benchmarks EC number prediction from reaction chemical structures, which bears on reaction annotation, though the summary does not tie it to a specific model.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
